I fixed #1176: the "treating unknown provider … as OpenAI-compatible" warning now prints once per run instead of five times. It's committed as 45265c95.

Where the copies came from. Only one place in src/ prints that warning: the fallback branch of create_model_config in src/agent_builder.rs. Its comment said parse_args and /provider "already warn", and that isn't true of the current code:
• parse_args only steps in when an unknown provider comes with no base URL, and then it refuses the run (#1103). With a URL it says nothing.
• /provider nosuch in the REPL is refused before any config gets built.

So whether the provider comes from the --provider flag or from .yoyo.toml, this line is the only notice the user gets. It ran on every model-config build, which is five times for one -p hi.

Fix. I kept the line and made it print once per (provider, base URL) pair per process, reusing the same once-only helper the guessed-limits note already uses (first_unknown_limits_warning). I also rewrote the comment to say what the code actually does now.

Checks:
• Probe on the rebuilt binary: grep -c "treating unknown provider" now gives 1 (it was 5).
• New test, `tests/unknown_provider_warning_once.rs`: runs the real binary in a temporary home and project directory, pointed at a dead local port so no real host is contacted. The flag case and the .yoyo.toml case each count exactly 1, and --provider openai counts 0.
• Positive control: I disabled the guard (marker count checked as 1 first). Both "exactly 1" rows failed by name with a count of 5. After restoring it the marker count was 0 and the test passed again.
• Full gate: cargo fmt, clippy -D warnings and cargo test all pass (7422 tests, 0 failed). tests/module_size.rs now lists agent_builder.rs at 5009 lines (was 4997).

One small mismatch: the helper's doc comment in model_limits_note.rs still says it records (provider, model), but here it gets (provider, URL). That file wasn't in this task, so I left it alone. My new comment in agent_builder.rs explains the reuse.

I didn't touch #1175 (which default model custom or unknown providers get).
